#X obj 60 578 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 606 1 float: note number. Velocity is taken from inlet 2 \;   and velocity 0 is a note off. \; 1 list: note \, velocity and \, if you like \, the MIDI channel. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages. \; 2 float: velocity for the next note \, 0 to 127 (default 100). \; 3 float or list: raw MIDI bytes \, as midiin gives them. \; 3 anything: a message \, the same set as inlet 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 732 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 760 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: info \, name \, 0-127 and value text for every \;   change \, the patch that plays \, its names \, the channels. \; 3 float: SysEx bytes for midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 854 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 882 name v: set a control \, in the values the D-50 shows. \; name: report it as info. \; n name v: set it from a pot or a MIDI CC \, 0 to 127. \; ninfo name: report it as info. \; preset n: a factory preset \, read only. \; user n: a slot of the user bank \, 0 to 63. \; init: a plain sawtooth patch to start from. \; reload: the same patch again \, edits dropped. \; store n: the playing patch into user slot n \, in memory. \; userwrite: write the user bank to d50user-bank.syx. \; userread: read it again. Both also take a file name. \; usersend: the user bank as SysEx on outlet 3. \; presets \, users: list the names. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bendrange. \; mod f: modulation lever \, 0 to 1. \; aftertouch f: channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; channel n: MIDI receive channel \, 0 is all. \; txchannel n: channel of the controller feedback and device \;   number of SysEx dumps \, 1 to 16. \; status: report patch \, names \, channels \, voices and CPU. \; stop: all notes off. \; reset: all notes off and the effect tails emptied., f 64;
#X obj 60 1264 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1292 midiin: raw bytes into inlet 3. d50~ takes notes \, bend \, \;   aftertouch \, program change \, CC 1 (lever) \, 5 (portamento \;   time) \, 7 (volume) \, 64 (hold) \, 65 (portamento) and SysEx. \; midiout: the floats of outlet 3 \, SysEx answers and dumps. \; d50cc 1: the CC pages 20 to 119 on channel 1. \; Without midiin: send note lists and bend \, mod \, sustain., f 64;
#X obj 60 1402 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1430 cut (0): cutoff of every synth partial \, also of notes that are sounding. 0 leaves the patch as it is. \; res (0): resonance of every synth partial \, for the notes that follow. \; att (0): attack (TVA time 1) of all four partials \, for the notes that follow. \; rel (0): release (TVA and TVF time 5) of all four partials \, for the notes that follow. \; chorus (patch): chorus balance of both tones. \; reverb (patch): reverb balance of the patch. \; balance (patch): balance of the two tones \, lower at 0 \, upper at 100. \; volume (80): master volume \, not stored in a patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 1652 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controller\ layer\ and\ editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1680 d50cc is the controller layer: MIDI CC 20 to 119 in pages of 8 \, the same pages as for pdoly8~ and tx81z~. Page 1 is the performance row \, page k is row k of the editor. It turns a CC into an n message and sends every change made elsewhere back to the controller as CC. Its argument is the MIDI channel \, and it follows the channels d50~ reports. \; d50edit is the editor: click it in the object area above. All 117 controls in rows of 8 \, the factory presets and the user bank \, the MIDI channels and SysEx. It explains itself in its readme. \; The D-50 has four partials \, two per tone. A partial name such as cutoff acts on the selected partial \, a tone name such as structure on the tone it belongs to. part 0 to 3 selects U1 \, U2 \, L1 \, L2. All names are listed at the end of this patch with their CC numbers., f 64;
#X obj 60 1934 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1962 The object contains no Roland data. It loads its files from the folder of the external \, or else from the folder of the patch. \; d50_pcm.bin: the PCM samples \, written by tools/make_d50_data.py from your own ROM images. Without it the object stays silent and says so in the Pd window. \; Every .syx file beside it is read as a factory bank \, a D-50 bulk dump of 64 patches. The files are loaded in alphabetical order \, PND50-00.syx first \, and their patches are numbered through. Without one the object plays eight built-in presets \, which cannot be edited. \; d50user-bank.syx: the user bank \, in the same format. Until it has been written the user bank holds 64 init patches. \; The engine runs at 32 kHz \, the rate of the original \, and is resampled to the rate of Pd., f 64;
#X obj 60 2216 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 2268 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2244 4 0 127 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2268 preset \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2244 4 0 63 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2268 user \$1;
#X obj 60 2304 r \$0-d50-out;
#X obj 60 2328 route preset user;
#X obj 60 2354 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 60 2382 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 100 2382 20 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 260 2354 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 260 2382 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 300 2382 20 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 82 2410 preset selects a factory preset \, user a slot of the user bank. The third outlet answers with the number and the name. \; A patch change sets the first four controls of the performance row (cut \, res \, att \, rel) back to 0. \; store 5 followed by userwrite keeps the playing patch in user slot 5 and on disk. The editor does both with save patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 2520 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Patch\ editing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2548 A few examples \, the editor has them all. Values are the ones the D-50 shows \, fine for example runs from -50 to 50. A name without a value reports the current one. \; A partial or tone edit is heard from the next note on. Chorus \, equalizer \, reverb and the balances follow at once \, and cut also moves the notes that are sounding. \; The built-in presets cannot be edited. Load a bank \, or start from init or a user slot., f 64;
#X obj 460 2704 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2680 6 0 3 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2704 part \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2680 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2704 cutoff \$1;
#X floatatom 260 2680 6 0 30 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 2704 reso \$1;
#X floatatom 360 2680 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 2704 level \$1;
#X text 82 2734 part (0): the partial that cutoff \, reso \, level and the other partial names act on. 0 to 3 are U1 \, U2 \, L1 \, L2. \; cutoff (patch): filter cutoff of the selected partial. Only synth partials have a filter \, a PCM partial ignores it. \; reso (patch): filter resonance. \; level (patch): level of the partial., f 64;
#X obj 460 2858 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2834 6 1 7 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2858 structure \$1;
#X text 82 2888 structure (patch): which partials of the tone are synth or PCM and whether they are ring modulated \, see Tone controls., f 64;
#X obj 460 2948 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2924 6 0 8 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2948 keymode \$1;
#X text 82 2978 keymode (patch): whole \, dual \, split and their solo variants \, see Patch controls., f 64;
#X obj 60 3024 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty By\ address 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3052 s \$0-d50;
#X msg 60 3052 l2 cutoff 30;
#X msg 190 3052 l2 cutoff;
#X msg 320 3052 dump;
#X msg 60 3086 param 13 60;
#X msg 190 3086 param 13;
#X msg 320 3086 sysexdump;
#X text 82 3120 l2 cutoff 30: section \, name and value set a parameter without changing the selection. The sections are u1 \, u2 \, upper \, l1 \, l2 \, lower and patch. Without a value the message reports it. \; dump: reports the three names and every named parameter of every section \, 311 messages. \; param a v: sets one of the 448 bytes of the patch by address \, with the value a D-50 dump stores. The address is the section times 64 plus the offset \, sections counted from 0 in the order above. param a reports the byte. \; name: patch name My Patch sets the patch name \, up to 18 characters. upper name and lower name take up to 10. \; sysexdump: sends the playing patch as SysEx \, see below., f 64;
#X obj 60 3326 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty SysEx 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3354 The object speaks the exclusive format of the D-50 \, so an editor or librarian made for the D-50 can program it \, and it can exchange patches with a real D-50. The bytes arrive with the rest of the MIDI at the third inlet and leave the third outlet as floats. \; Data set (DT1) to address 00-00-00 edits the playing patch \, the same 448 bytes that param reaches. Data set to 02-00-00 \, the internal memory of the D-50 \, goes to the user bank: a bulk dump replaces it in memory \, userwrite keeps it. \; A request (RQ1) for either area is answered at the third outlet. sysexdump sends the playing patch and usersend the user bank without being asked. \; sysex followed by the bytes of one message does the same from a list. The device number of incoming messages is not checked \, answers carry the number of the request., f 64;
#X obj 60 3608 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Playing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3660 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3636 6 -1 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3660 bend \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3636 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 3660 mod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 3636 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 3660 aftertouch \$1;
#X floatatom 360 3636 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 3660 sustain \$1;
#X text 82 3690 bend (0): pitch wheel \, -1 to 1. The range in semitones is bendrange. \; mod (0): modulation lever \, 0 to 1. What it does is part of the patch. \; aftertouch (0): channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain (0): hold pedal. Notes released while it is 1 sound until it returns to 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 3816 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Additional\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3868 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3844 6 -50 50 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3868 tune \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3844 6 1 8 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 3868 voices \$1;
#X text 82 3898 tune (0): master tune in cents. \; voices (8): polyphony per tone. A patch that uses one tone plays twice as many notes., f 64;
#X obj 460 3974 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3950 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3974 governor \$1;
#X text 82 4004 governor (0): when 1 \, the object ends the oldest released note early whenever a block takes longer to compute than it lasts. Held notes are never ended. Meant for small machines such as Bela., f 64;
#X obj 60 4082 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Performance\ and\ setup\ controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4110 cut -63..63 \, CC 20: cutoff of every synth partial \, also of \;   notes that are sounding. 0 leaves the patch as it is \; res -63..63 \, CC 21: resonance of every synth partial \, for the \;   notes that follow \; att -63..63 \, CC 22: attack (TVA time 1) of all four partials \, \;   for the notes that follow \; rel -63..63 \, CC 23: release (TVA and TVF time 5) of all four \;   partials \, for the notes that follow \; chorus 0..100 \, CC 24: chorus balance of both tones \; reverb 0..100 \, CC 25: reverb balance of the patch \; balance 0..100 \, CC 26: balance of the two tones \, lower at 0 \, \;   upper at 100 \; volume 0..100 \, CC 27: master volume \, not stored in a patch \; part 0..3 \, CC 28: the partial the partial names act on \, and \;   with it the tone (U1 U2: upper \, L1 L2: lower) \; tune -50..50: master tune in cents \, not stored in a patch \; voices 1..8: polyphony per tone \, not stored in a patch, f 64;
#X obj 60 4396 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Partial\ controls:\ the\ selected\ partial 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4424 coarse 0..72 \, CC 29: pitch in semitones \, 0 is C1 \; fine -50..50 \, CC 30: fine tune \; keyfollow 0..16 \, CC 31: pitch keyfollow step \, 11 is a semitone \;   per key \; lfomode 0..3: pitch LFO: off \, + \, - \, aftertouch and lever \; penvmode 0..2: pitch envelope: off \, + \, - \; bendmode 0..2: bender: off \, keyfollow \, normal \; wave 0..1 \, CC 33: synth waveform: square \, sawtooth \; pcm 1..100 \, CC 34: PCM sample \; pw 0..100 \, CC 35: pulse width \; pwvelo -7..7: pulse width by velocity \; pwlfo 0..5: pulse width LFO: +1 \, -1 \, +2 \, -2 \, +3 \, -3 \; pwlfodepth 0..100 \, CC 36: pulse width LFO depth \; pwat -7..7: pulse width by aftertouch \; cutoff 0..100 \, CC 37: filter cutoff \; reso 0..30 \, CC 39: filter resonance \; tvfkf 0..14 \, CC 40: cutoff keyfollow step \; tvfbiaspoint 0..127: cutoff bias point and direction \; tvfbiaslevel -7..7: cutoff bias level \; tvfenv 0..100 \, CC 41: filter envelope depth \; tvfvelo 0..100 \, CC 42: filter envelope depth by velocity \; tvfdepthkf 0..4: filter envelope depth keyfollow \; tvftimekf 0..4: filter envelope time keyfollow \; tvft1 to tvft5 0..100 \, CC 46 to 50: filter envelope times \; tvfl1 to tvfl3 0..100 \, CC 51 to 53: filter envelope levels \; tvfsustain 0..100 \, CC 43: filter envelope sustain level \; tvfend 0..1: filter envelope end level: 0 \, 100 \; tvflfo 0..5: filter LFO \, as pwlfo \; tvflfodepth 0..100 \, CC 44: filter LFO depth \; tvfat -7..7 \, CC 45: cutoff by aftertouch \; level 0..100 \, CC 54: level of the partial \; velo -50..50 \, CC 55: level by velocity \; tvabiaspoint 0..127 \, CC 59: level bias point and direction \; tvabiaslevel -12..0 \, CC 60: level bias level \; tvat1 to tvat5 0..100 \, CC 62 to 72: level envelope times \; tval1 to tval3 0..100 \, CC 73 to 75: level envelope levels \; tvasustain 0..100 \, CC 56: level envelope sustain level \; tvaend 0..1: level envelope end level: 0 \, 100 \; tvavelofollow 0..4 \, CC 61: level envelope time 1 by velocity \; tvatimekf 0..4: level envelope time keyfollow \; tvalfo 0..5: level LFO \, as pwlfo \; tvalfodepth 0..100 \, CC 57: level LFO depth \; tvaat -7..7 \, CC 58: level by aftertouch, f 64;
#X obj 60 5126 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Tone\ controls:\ its\ tone 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5154 structure 1..7 \, CC 76: S+S \, S+S ring \, P+S \, P+S ring \, S+P ring \, \;   P+P \, P+P ring \; penvvelo 0..2 \, CC 82: pitch envelope by velocity \; penvtimekf 0..4 \, CC 83: pitch envelope time keyfollow \; penvt1 to penvt4 0..50 \, CC 85 to 89: pitch envelope times \; penvl0 to penvl2 -50..50 \, CC 90 to 92: pitch envelope levels \; penvsustain -50..50 \, CC 93: pitch envelope sustain level \; penvend -50..50: pitch envelope end level \; pmodlfo 0..100 \, CC 79: pitch LFO depth \; pmodlever 0..100 \, CC 80: pitch LFO depth by the lever \; pmodat 0..100 \, CC 81: pitch LFO depth by aftertouch \; lfo1wave 0..3 \, CC 94: triangle \, sawtooth \, square \, random \; lfo1rate 0..100 \, CC 95: LFO 1 rate \; lfo1delay 0..100 \, CC 102: LFO 1 delay \; lfo1sync 0..2 \, CC 103: off \, on \, key \; lfo2wave 0..3 \, CC 104: as lfo1wave \; lfo2rate 0..100 \, CC 105: LFO 2 rate \; lfo2delay 0..100 \, CC 106: LFO 2 delay \; lfo2sync 0..1 \, CC 107: off \, on \; lfo3wave 0..3 \, CC 108: as lfo1wave \; lfo3rate 0..100 \, CC 109: LFO 3 rate \; lfo3delay 0..100 \, CC 110: LFO 3 delay \; lfo3sync 0..1 \, CC 111: off \, on \; eqlowfreq 0..15 \, CC 112: low shelf frequency step \; eqlowgain -12..12 \, CC 113: low shelf gain in dB \; eqhighfreq 0..21 \, CC 114: high band frequency step \; eqhighq 0..8 \, CC 119: high band width step \; eqhighgain -12..12 \, CC 115: high band gain in dB \; chorustype 1..8 \, CC 116: chorus type \; chorusrate 0..100 \, CC 117: chorus rate \; chorusdepth 0..100 \, CC 118: chorus depth \; tchorus 0..100: chorus balance of this tone \; mute 0..3 \, CC 78: partials sounding: none \, first \, second \, both \; pbal 0..100 \, CC 77: balance of the two partials, f 64;
#X obj 60 5712 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Patch\ controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5740 keymode 0..8: whole \, dual \, split \, whole solo \, dual solo \, split \;   upper solo \, split lower solo \, separate \, separate solo \; split 0..60: split point \, 0 is C2 \; portamode 0..2: portamento on upper \, lower \, both \; ukeyshift to lkeyshift -24..24: key shift of each tone in \;   semitones \; ufine to lfine -50..50: fine tune of each tone \; bendrange 0..12: bender range in semitones \; atbend -12..12: pitch bend by aftertouch in semitones \; portatime 0..100: portamento time \; outmode 1..4: how the tones go to reverb and outputs \; reverbtype 1..32: reverb type \; reverb 0..100 \, CC 25: reverb balance \; pvol 0..100: level of the patch \, volume is the master \; balance 0..100 \, CC 26: balance of the two tones \; porta 0..1: portamento switch, f 64;
